# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} Engineering Agents — Claude Code Handoff

Orchestration layer for the **code** arm of {{PROJECT_NAME}}. This context turns the Figma design system
and the validated screens into **shipping software**: the one coded component library ({{COMPONENT_LIB}})
+ Storybook, the native app ({{NATIVE_STACK}}), and the store release. It is the third context alongside
`{{DS_REPO}}` (Figma DS) and `{{STUDIO_REPO}}` (Figma screens + prototype).

---

## The organizing principle — one coded library, three consumers

The Figma DS is authored in `{{DS_REPO}}`. **This** context builds its ONE code implementation and ships
it. `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` is consumed by (1) Storybook, (2) the usability prototype (Expo web export on
Vercel), and (3) the native app — so the thing you usability-test is the thing you ship. That shared
library is what makes prototype→app rework near-zero.

| Role | Write surface | Owns (object type) |
|---|---|---|
| `component-engineer` | `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` — `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` (RN components + coded tokens) + Storybook | the CODE mirror of {{SYSTEM_NAME}} — token sync from the Figma DS, components, stories, code↔Figma parity |
| `app-engineer` | `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` — the native app ({{NATIVE_STACK}}, `{{APP_PACKAGE_ID}}`) | screens composed from the shared library · navigation · storage/state · native modules · device verification |
| `build-uploader` | `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` — build/release config, store metadata, submission | the signed artifact · versioning · data-safety/privacy declarations · `eas submit` + track promotion |

**Mental model:** `component-engineer` codes the DS as `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` (token-synced, Storybook-
verified) → the studio's prototype and `app-engineer`'s app both consume it → `app-engineer` wires native
concerns onto the validated screens → `build-uploader` builds, uploads, and CONFIRMS the release. A Figma
DS gap routes to `{{DS_REPO}}`; a design/flow change routes to `{{STUDIO_REPO}}`.

