## Slash commands (thin wrappers — they delegate, they don't duplicate)

| Command | Delegates to | Does |
|---|---|---|
| `/component-build [component / "sync"]` | `component-engineer` | build/extend a coded component + story, or re-sync tokens from the Figma DS |
| `/app-build [screen / flow]` | `app-engineer` | compose the shared library into a validated screen + wire native concerns |
| `/release ["build" / "upload" / "promote" / track]` | `build-uploader` | build the signed artifact, submit, and confirm the track |

Each command body only *invokes the agent* — the workflow lives in one place. Add new commands the same
way: thin, delegating — never duplicate.

---

## Separate contexts — design + screens

By design, this context is **code only**. The Figma design system (tokens, components, publish, drift)
lives in `{{DS_REPO}}`; the Figma screens + the usability prototype + the validation gate live in
`{{STUDIO_REPO}}`. `DESIGN.md` is shared ground truth all three read. This context consumes the published
Figma DS (as coded tokens/components) and the validated screens (as the app's spec), and produces the
shipping app.
